n continuing is the whole of the contract — a client that does it needs nothing else from this document.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a14 version carried; more concise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b16\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a15 version carried; equivalent meaning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b17\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in. It names the cap and the tier as well.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a16 and a17 versions carried.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b18\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"None of those fields is a substitute for the header, and a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a18 version carried; clearer phrasing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b19\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused — nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a19 version carried; equivalent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b20\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## How to retry well\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base heading chosen; decision made above.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b21\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a21 version carried; equivalent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b22\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"1. Honour the header, every time. The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path. A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see. There is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a22-a25 rule 1 carried; clearer framing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b27\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"2. Retry only what is safe to retry. A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path. The four cases are not interchangeable. A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive. Avoid writing that loop.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a26-a30 rule 2 carried; more direct wording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b31\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"3. Batch is different. A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window. The tier is set on the credential when it is issued and cannot be asked for per call. Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a31-a34 rule 3 carried; base document structure kept.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b34\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"4. Log every refusal seen. A caller that cannot say how often it was refused last week cannot argue for a larger cap, and nobody at the far end will assemble that argument on its behalf. The log line should carry the credential, the window and the wait.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a35-a37 rule 4 carried; equivalent guidance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b37\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Other refusals and their codes\",\n      \"reason\": \"a38 heading carried; base structure maintained.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b38\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons and only one of them is the one above.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a40 version carried; more specific phrasing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b39\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The distinction matters to a retry loop. A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service — and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Distinction between traffic and non-traffic refusals covered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b40\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a41 version carried; equivalent statement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b41\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The distinction matters to a retry loop. A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service — and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals. Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to is what separates the two cases, and it costs one comparison.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Why distinction matters covered in a43-a45.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b42\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service — and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a44 version carried; same content.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b44\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all, which is the outcome everyone prefers.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a50 version carried; directly addresses the point.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b46\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A cap can be raised, but only with measurement. Bring a week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Measurement requirement covered in a46-a48.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b47\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Bring a week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a48 version carried; equivalent statement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b48\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty — a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a49 version carried; both state the same evaluation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b50\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel, and they are answered within two working days.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a51 version carried; includes both the channel and timeline.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b51\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"There is no expedited path and no exception list.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a52 version carried; same statement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b52\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel, and they are answered within two working days. There is no expedited path and no exception list.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a51 and a52 together cover timeline and process.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\"\n}\n```","ttft_ms":167908,"type":"result","duration_ms":193218,"uuid":"94e2d64b-d9f6-4fdf-b7b3-950abe7279ec","ttft_stream_ms":990,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":990,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
